==English==
{{was wotd|2024|June|21}}

===Etymology===
{{uncertain|en|Origin uncertain}}; possible sources which have been suggested include the following:<ref>{{R:OED Online|subentry=to face the music|subpos=phrase|entry=face|pos=v|id=1135211797|date=March 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=phrase|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220823012052/https://www.lexico.com/definition/face_the_music}}</ref>

* A performer on a stage facing the music from the orchestra pit when confronting a possibly hostile audience.
* The historical act of a soldier who was dishonourably discharged from military service being paraded in front of other soldiers to the sound of a drum or music.
* A soldier facing the noise of battle (''music'' being military slang for the sound of gunfire or other ordnance).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌfeɪs ðə ˈmjuːzɪk/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌfeɪs ðə ˈmjuzɪk/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-face the music.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːzɪk|s=4}}
* {{hyphenation|en|face the mus|ic}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[accept#Verb|accept]] or [[confront]] the [[unpleasant]] [[consequence#Noun|consequences]] of one's [[action#Noun|actions]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#: {{synonyms|en|face up to|pay the penalty|pay the price}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|year=2013|author=w:Rockstar Games|title=w:Grand Theft Auto V|system=|level=The Paleto Score|scene=Exiting a robbed bank surrounded by police with [[minigun]] and [[ballistic]] [[suit]]|text='''{{w|Trevor Philips}} ({{w|Steven Ogg}})''': Time to '''face the music'''!}}

